<title>EGYPT: EgyptAir has clearance for Libyan pilgrim flights.</title>
<headline>EgyptAir has clearance for Libyan pilgrim flights.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.N. sanctions committee has given the Egyptian national carrier EgyptAir permission to fly Libyan pilgrims to Saudi Arabia for the annual pilgrimage to Mecca in April, government newspapers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>EgyptAir will make 90 return flights between Tripoli or Benghazi and Jeddah, carrying 11,000 Libyans, they said.</p>
<p>The United Nations has banned flights to and from Libya since 1992 because the Libyan authorities refuse to hand over two men accused of blowing up an American airliner over the Scottish town of Lockerbie in December 1988.</p>
<p>But the sanctions committee can waive the ban in special cases. It allowed EgyptAir to fly Libyan pilgrims to Saudi Arabia in both of the two previous years.</p>
</text>
